# Bundled upstream manifests are pinned by SHA-256 over their exact bytes
# (see backend/api/services/cluster_build/{cni,addons}/*.py) and verified at
# runtime before they are applied to a cluster. A CRLF checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) changes those bytes, fails the integrity
# check, and would ship broken bundles into any image built from that
# checkout. Keep them byte-for-byte as committed: no line-ending conversion.
backend/api/data/** -text

# The vSphere provider patch is applied with `git apply` inside a Linux image
# build; a CRLF checkout would make it fail to apply. Keep it byte-for-byte.
backend/tofu/*.patch -text
